## 14. Security Considerations

- Passwords must be hashed before being stored.
- JWT secrets and MongoDB credentials must remain private.
- Environment files must not be committed to GitHub.
- Task endpoints must enforce ownership on the backend.
- Protected routes must reject invalid or missing tokens.
- Production CORS settings should allow only the intended frontend origins.
- Screenshots and documentation must not expose private credentials or tokens.

